{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-06T09:14:18.568Z","data":{"text":"I implemented task 3.\n\n## Summary\n\n**`src/core/vcs/checkout-root.ts` (new)** — `resolveCheckoutRoot(cwd, config)` returns the main checkout when `cwd` is a linked worktree whose HEAD is on an `osq/` branch and the first `worktreeList()` entry is a different path, comparing paths after `fs.realpath`. It uses `selectVcs`, `root()`, `head()`, and `worktreeList()`, and falls back to `cwd` on every error path so it never throws.\n\n**`src/cli/approve.ts`** — `approveCommand` now resolves the checkout first, reloads the checkout's config with `loadConfig` when it moved and no config was passed, prints `Approving from the checkout <path>` to `inputs.stderr` when it moved, and uses the resolved path for `approveSpec`, `findChange`, and `readNextStep`.\n\n**`tests/approve-from-worktree.test.ts` (new)** — covers the three \"Approve from a worktree\" scenarios through `approveCommand` (plus symlink and fallback cases).\n\nVerification:\n- Task verify: 21 tests pass.\n- `pnpm verify`: typechecks, build, full test suite, and lint all pass.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/152-halt-self-recovery/.run/results/3.md`.\n\nTouched: src/core/vcs/checkout-root.ts, src/cli/approve.ts, tests/approve-from-worktree.test.ts"}}
